---
import FeaturedLessons from '../components/FeaturedLessons.astro';
import LearningRoutes from '../components/LearningRoutes.astro';
import BookLayout from '../layouts/BookLayout.astro';

import modelSnapshot from '../data/commercial-model-snapshot.json';
import { chapters } from '../data/chapters.js';
import { servingGuide, shortArticlePaths } from '../data/site.js';
import { withBasePath, withPagePath } from '../utils/paths.js';
---

<BookLayout title="Home" lang="en">
  <h1>Foundation Model Engineering</h1>
  <p>A free English and Korean textbook on training, serving, and evaluating foundation models, with browser experiments and CPU PyTorch labs.</p>

  <section aria-labelledby="short-reads">
    <h2 id="short-reads">Short reads</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={withPagePath(shortArticlePaths.bucketing)}>Why length bucketing cut padding but left peak KV memory unchanged</a></li>
      <li><a href={withPagePath(shortArticlePaths.loop)}>Why one more token shrank a KV cache buffer</a></li>
      <li><a href={withPagePath(shortArticlePaths.whisper)}>How an 11-second recording became 30 seconds for Whisper</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <FeaturedLessons lang="en" />

  <h2>Model selection and cost</h2>
  <p>Explore the November 25 benchmark results in the comparison of <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-17/commercial-model-benchmarks')}>{modelSnapshot.models.length} model profiles</a>. Check how to access <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-17/commercial-model-benchmarks') + '#model-glm-54'}>GLM-5.4</a>, find the context limit in the public <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-17/commercial-model-benchmarks') + '#ling-32-air-context'}>Ling-3.2-air checkpoint</a>, or calculate what one extra input token can do to the <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-17/commercial-model-benchmarks') + '#long-context-cost'}>GPT-6.2 Astra and Sol bill</a>. <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-11/audio-and-speech-integration')}>Speech</a>, <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-11/image-diffusion-models')}>image</a> and <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-11/commercial-video-models')}>video models</a> have their own evaluation chapters.</p>

  <LearningRoutes lang="en" />

  <h2>Train a small decoder on a CPU</h2>
  <p>A decoder learns to repeat four symbols. On the held-out sequence <code>12 13 16 14</code>, its first prediction is 7. Will the same error come back four steps later? <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-7/tiny-decoder-lab') + '#decoder-copy-trace'}>Follow one prediction token by token</a>, <a href="https://nbviewer.org/urls/sungeuns.github.io/foundation-model-engineering/labs/2026-11/tiny-decoder-worked-en.ipynb#cell-id=compare-results">compare test losses with and without earlier tokens</a>, or <a href="https://mybinder.org/v2/gh/sungeuns/foundation-model-engineering/b6a54ff80e80cbf10d68b15d4419bbae2269ef7e?urlpath=lab%2Ftree%2Fpublic%2Flabs%2Ftiny-decoder-lab.ipynb">run it on Binder</a> without an account. For local Jupyter, <a href={withBasePath('/labs/tiny-decoder-lab.ipynb')} download="tiny-decoder-lab.ipynb">download the notebook</a>.</p>

  <h2>About the book</h2>
  <p id="serving-guide"><a href={servingGuide.downloads.en} type="application/epub+zip">Download <em>LLM Serving in Practice</em> (EPUB)</a> to read three lessons offline. Revision 3 follows a measured KV cache from 990 to 1,350 KiB, shows when each request gets a turn, and traces the pause between streamed tokens. All 16 quizzes include answers.</p>
  <p>Seongeun So maintains the book. The first Korean edition was translated from English with help from Gemini. Recent labs include code and measurements produced with Codex. Each lesson is revised in English first, with its code and worked examples updated in Korean in the same change. Browse <a href="#book-contents">all {chapters.reduce((n, chapter) => n + chapter.subs.length, 0)} lessons</a> or <a href="https://github.com/sungeuns/foundation-model-engineering">bookmark the repository on GitHub</a>. If an example behaves differently from the explanation, <a href="https://github.com/sungeuns/foundation-model-engineering/issues/new/choose">report the chapter and the inputs that reproduce it</a>.</p>
  <p class="last-update">Last update <time datetime="2026-11-25">2026-11-25</time></p>

  <h2 id="book-contents">Table of Contents</h2>
  <div class="toc">
    {chapters.map(ch => (
      <div class="toc-chapter">
        <h3 id={`chapter-${ch.id}`}>
          <a href={`#chapter-${ch.id}`}>{ch.title.en}</a>
          <small>({ch.subs.length} {ch.subs.length === 1 ? 'lesson' : 'lessons'})</small>
        </h3>
        <ul>
          {ch.subs.map(sub => (
            <li><a href={withPagePath(sub.path)}>{sub.title.en}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

</BookLayout>

<style>
  .last-update { color: var(--secondary-color); font-size: .9rem; }
  .toc {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .toc-chapter {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .toc h3 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--text-color);
    scroll-margin-top: 4rem;
  }
  .toc h3 a { color: inherit; }
  .toc h3 small { font-size: .88rem; font-weight: normal; color: var(--secondary-color); }
  .toc ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }
  .toc li {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .toc a {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--accent-color);
  }
  .toc a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
